    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d53-a3">

                <pb facs="0216" n="196" sameAs="frus:frus1864p2/pg196"/>

                <head ana="#head_untitled-missing-head-in-printed-volume">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">“Hindley Hall, near
                            Wigan,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-06-24"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 24, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>“<hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir:</hi> I am in due receipt of your esteemed
                    favor of the 21st instant, and am gratified to find that the timely aid we
                    rendered with the yacht Deer-hound to the gallant captain and officers and crew
                    of the Alabama has met with your approval. 1 shall always look back to that
                    event with satisfaction, however much we may regret the result which
                    necessitated my interference.</p>
                <p>“Yours, very respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>“JOHN LANCASTER.”</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. J. M. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mason</hi>.”</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
